{
  "about": "What each example must produce, written on 2026-11-16 before its first run. Per run: the exit code; stdout and stderr facts: `lines` (each must be a whole line of the output, leading and trailing spaces ignored), `contains` (substrings), `absent` (substrings that must not appear), `startCounts` (how many lines may start with the text, after leading spaces), `empty`, and `sameAs` (the run's output must equal another run's). The byte-for-byte outputs are pinned in examples/<example>/expected/<run>.stdout and .stderr from the first run that met these facts; test/examples/examples.test.ts compares every offline run with both. `{tmp}` is a fresh temporary directory per run. Every run is made with node alone on PATH (helm and kustomize not found), from the repository root.",
  "edits": [
    {
      "example": "declared",
      "run": "without-edge",
      "what": "stdout fact \"Cycles: 0\" replaced by \"Cycles: none found among 8 nodes and 11 edges read\"",
      "why": "first run, 2026-11-16: crankpath never states a no-cycle result as a bare count; it says none were found among the nodes and edges it read (the honesty rule). My expected wording was wrong; the result (no cycle without the declared edge) was as expected."
    },
    {
      "example": "opaque",
      "run": "text",
      "what": "stdout facts: \"at least 2 of 3 sources opaque\" became \"at least 3 of 4\", \"alias-limit\" became \"reason: limit\" and \"alias expansion over the limit\"; the suggestion and the absence of \"which no readable source defines\" added; a JSON run added",
      "why": "first run, 2026-11-16: (1) the alias-bomb file lies under Application argocd/web's source path, so that Application is itself opaque, reason limit (a source with a file it could not read is not fully seen), which I had not expected; (2) the text names a file's outcome in words (the JSON run now asserts the word alias-limit); (3) the estate was edited after that run: the first run showed the HelmRepository and the encrypted Secret as defined by no readable source, because no source deployed platform/monitoring, which hid what the example is for; Application argocd/monitoring (apps/monitoring.yaml) now deploys that directory, so the sources are 4."
    },
    {
      "example": "refusals",
      "run": "text",
      "what": "stdout fact \"too-large\" replaced by \"(too large)\"; a JSON run added that asserts too-large, symlink and invalid-name",
      "why": "first run, 2026-11-16: the text names a file's outcome in words, the JSON by its word; the result (the file refused as over the size limit) was as expected."
    },
    {
      "example": "opaque",
      "run": "text",
      "what": "stdout fact \"alias expansion over the limit\" shortened to \"(alias expansion over\"",
      "why": "second run, 2026-11-16, after the edit above: the text wraps that phrase at 80 columns, so the whole phrase is not one substring; my fact was copied without the line break. Nothing else differed."
    },
    {
      "example": "refusals",
      "run": "text",
      "what": "the estate, not the expectation: the symlink platform/web/escape.yaml now points at an existing file (examples/thin-slice/repo/platform/gitea/config.yaml); its first target was one directory short and named nothing",
      "why": "after the first runs, 2026-11-16: Biome reported the link as broken. crankpath never follows a symlink, so the output is the same either way: the examples lane gave byte-identical output before and after the change (21 of 21 runs)."
    }
  ],
  "examples": {
    "thin-slice": {
      "lane": "offline",
      "what": "the thin-slice cycle: an Argo CD Application reads its Git source from the Gitea it deploys",
      "runs": [
        {
          "name": "text",
          "args": [
            "examples/thin-slice/repo",
            "--repo-url",
            "http://gitea-http.gitea:3000/ops/thin-slice"
          ],
          "exit": 0,
          "stdout": {
            "lines": [
              "Run status: ANALYSED",
              "Cycles: 1 uncranked"
            ],
            "contains": [
              "label: extracted  nodes: 5",
              "Not startable from a cold start: 7 of 7 nodes"
            ],
            "absent": [
              "\u001b"
            ]
          },
          "stderr": {
            "empty": true
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "json",
          "args": [
            "examples/thin-slice/repo",
            "--repo-url",
            "http://gitea-http.gitea:3000/ops/thin-slice",
            "--format",
            "json"
          ],
          "exit": 0,
          "stdout": {
            "lines": [
              "\"state\": \"ANALYSED\"",
              "\"label\": \"extracted\",",
              "\"schemaVersion\": 1,"
            ],
            "absent": [
              "\u001b"
            ]
          },
          "stderr": {
            "empty": true
          }
        }
      ]
    },
